# Build and tooling
/target
node_modules/
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Generated reports and diagnostic output.
#
# awsdiag's whole output is real log content, account ids, ARNs and instance
# ids from a live environment. Everything it can write goes here, matched
# loosely on purpose: the failure mode is committing an incident's data to a
# public repo, so a false positive costs nothing and a miss costs a lot.
*.html
!assets/*.html
*findings*.json
*.ndjson
*.csv
*.log

# Credential material. The tool resolves and caches AWS credentials, and a
# past defect wrote them to a *relative* path when HOME was unset -- plausibly
# a checked-out repository. This is the second line of defence behind the
# fixed code and GitHub push protection.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials
.aws/

# Design notes kept locally, not published.
docs/superpowers/

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
